    {
      "id": "A1-05-l2",
      "position": 2,
      "skill": "grammar",
      "title": "he works / she doesn't work",
      "est_minutes": 30,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "نستخدم **المضارع البسيط (present simple)** للعمل اليومي والعادات. مع **I, you, we, they** يبقى الفعل كما هو: «I **work**». أما مع **he, she, it** (أو اسم شخص واحد) **فنضيف s** إلى الفعل:\n\n- I work ← He **works**.\n- They teach ← She **teaches**.\n- I go ← He **goes**. / I do ← She **does**. / I have ← He **has**."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "youtube_id": "gBhK2m_CdQc",
          "video_title": "تكملة كلمات الوظائف — الحلقة 5",
          "channel": "ZAmericanEnglish",
          "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@ZAmericanEnglish",
          "duration_sec": 733,
          "optional": true,
          "approx_size_mb": 49
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "الصيغة",
            "مثال"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "إثبات",
              "he / she / it + فعل + s",
              "My father works at the port."
            ],
            [
              "نفي",
              "doesn't + الفعل (بدون s)",
              "She doesn't work on Friday."
            ],
            [
              "سؤال",
              "Does + الفاعل + الفعل (بدون s)؟",
              "Does he drive a bus?"
            ],
            [
              "إجابة",
              "Yes, he does. / No, he doesn't.",
              "Does she teach English? — Yes, she does."
            ],
            [
              "سؤال بأداة",
              "What / Where + does + …؟",
              "Where does your mother work?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "markdown_ar": "**قواعد إضافة s:**\n\n- معظم الأفعال: **s** ← works, drives.\n- بعد s, sh, ch, x, o: **es** ← teaches, washes, goes, does.\n- ساكن + y: **ies** ← study ← studies.\n\n**مهم:** بعد **doesn't** و **Does** يرجع الفعل بدون s: «He doesn't **work**.» وليس «doesn't works»."
        },
        {
